1. Explosion source: Set COUPLING_TYPE=3 and SINGLE_FORCE_ENZ=-1. The first CMTSOLUTION component is interpreted as the explosion moment magnitude. Internally, it is treated as an Mrr component, converted from z-r-t to x−y−z coordinates and back again. Although these coordinate conversions are unnecessary for a purely scalar explosion source, they are retained to keep the source-handling framework uniform across all source types. The explosion moment magnitude remains unchanged through this process. This approach uses the fact that the r direction in Mrr represents the local vertical direction, which corresponds z direction of Mzz in the z-r-t coordinate system. Note that this equivalence does not hold for the N-E or r-t components.

2. For fluid-solid interface (i.e., ICB and CMB) topography, the code may have problem for identifying which domain (fluid or solid) the element belongs to.
The reason is that the curvature is so large that even the centroid location is not enough for correctly identification (error due to curvature
is larger than half mesh size). To address this issue, either smooth the topography or make smaller element size.


